`makeMemberSummary` validates and converts a member into a display-safe value. Trim `handle`, `contact`, `note`, and `icon`. A blank handle or contact throws `RangeError`. A null or blank icon becomes the exact string `default-icon`. Roles are trimmed, blank roles discarded, duplicates removed, and the remaining roles sorted using ordinary code-point ordering. The function must not mutate the member or its roles array. The result and its roles array must be newly allocated.

Known-bad source:

```ts
export interface Member {
  readonly handle: string;
  readonly contact: string;
  readonly note: string;
  readonly icon: string | null;
  readonly roles: readonly string[];
}

export interface MemberSummary {
  readonly title: string;
  readonly contact: string;
  readonly note: string;
  readonly icon: string;
  readonly roles: string[];
}

export function makeMemberSummary(member: Member): MemberSummary {
  const title = member.handle.trim();
  const contact = member.contact.trim();
  if (title.length === 0 || contact.length === 0) throw new RangeError("handle and contact are required");
  const icon = member.icon === null ? "default-icon" : member.icon.trim();
  const roles = Array.from(new Set(member.roles.map((role) => role.trim()).filter(Boolean))).sort();
  return { title, contact, note: member.note.trim(), icon, roles };
}
```

